# Goal: foxes hunt more chickens, but chickens never die out (notes.md).
# The built-in world (scenarios/default.scenario: its terrain and starts) on
# 256x256, for 32 days, on 8 seeds: past the founders' wave (they die of age
# from day 6) and past a boom and bust of their kits, which the first 16 days
# hid (notes.md, experiment 10). Kills are taken from the 32-day baseline of
# the rules as of 1b76f0c (runs/11-32d.csv): above its best seed. The floors
# are the 16-day goal's, over the whole month.
# `chicken` is the family (hens and chicks), as in the rules; eggs are not.
rules ../../rules
seed 42
seeds 8
pass 7
size 256 256
terrain water_scale 12 water_level 0.30 rock_on_soil 0.04 rock_on_water 0.01
start chicken 1 / 400
start fox     1 / 5000
start flower  1 / 250
start hive    1 / 20000
start grass   1 / 20
start seed    1 / 100

run 32d
expect mean eaten chicken by fox per day >= 37 from 2d   # hunt more: above that baseline's best seed (36.7; 22.2 .. 36.7, median 30)
expect mean eaten chicken by fox per day >= 40 from 9d   # and all month: above its best (39.6; 19.4 .. 39.6, median 29.4)
expect always count chicken >= 100 from 2d               # never die out: half the 16-day baseline's usual lowest (200); that baseline: 0 .. 86
expect always count fox >= 3 from 2d                     # nor do the hunters: that baseline's foxes die out on all 8 seeds
